+    "reference/desc.md": "# Sigmoid 算子 API 描述\n\n## 1. 算子简介\n\nSigmoid 算子对输入张量完成 Sigmoid 运算，将任意实数映射到 (0, 1) 区间。\n\n**主要应用场景**：\n- 二分类任务的输出层激活\n- 门控机制（LSTM、GRU 等 RNN 中的门控信号）\n- 注意力权重计算\n- 概率输出的归一化\n\n**算子特征**：\n- 难度等级：L1（Elementwise）\n- 单输入单输出，逐元素运算，输出 shape 与输入完全一致\n- 支持 ND 格式输入\n\n## 2. 算子定义\n\n### 数学公式\n\n$$\ny = \\frac{1}{1 + e^{-x}}\n$$\n\n### 特殊情况\n\n| 输入 | 输出 |\n|------|------|\n| x = 0 | y = 0.5 |\n| x → +∞ | y → 1 |\n| x → -∞ | y → 0 |\n\n## 3. 接口规范\n\n### 算子原型\n\n```python\ncann_bench.sigmoid(Tensor x) -> Tensor y\n```\n\n### 输入参数说明\n\n| 参数 | 类型 | 默认值 | 描述 |\n|------|------|--------|------|\n| x | Tensor | 必选 | 输入张量，支持 ND 格式 |\n\n### 输出\n\n| 参数 | Shape | dtype | 描述 |\n|------|-------|-------|------|\n| y | 与输入 x 相同 | 与输入 x 相同 | Sigmoid 激活结果 |\n\n### 数据类型\n\n| 输入 dtype | 输出 dtype |\n|-----------|-----------|\n| float16 | float16 |\n| float32 | float32 |\n| bfloat16 | bfloat16 |\n\n### 规则与约束\n\n- 输出 shape 与输入 shape 完全一致，输出 dtype 与输入 dtype 一致\n- 无额外属性参数\n\n### 支持范围\n\n输入 tensor 各维度与参数的支持范围：\n\n| 维度 / 参数 | 范围 | 备注 |\n|---|---|---|\n| `x` 维度数 (ndim) | 1 ~ 8 | cases.csv 实测 1 ~ 5 |\n| `x` 单维大小 | 1 ~ 16384 | cases.csv 实测 2 ~ 8193 |\n| `x` 总元素数 | 1 ~ 64M | cases.csv 实测 ~1M ~ 64M  |\n\n约束：输出 shape 与输入 shape 完全一致，无 broadcasting；无额外属性。\n\n## 4. 精度要求\n\n采用[生态算子精度标准](https://gitcode.com/cann/opbase/blob/master/docs/zh/ops_precision_standard/experimental_standard.md)进行验证。\n\n**误差指标**：\n\n1. 平均相对误差（MERE）：采样点中相对误差平均值\n\n   $$\n   \\text{MERE} = \\text{avg}(\\frac{\\text{abs}(actual - golden)}{\\text{abs}(golden)+\\text{1e-7}})\n   $$\n\n2. 最大相对误差（MARE）：采样点中相对误差最大值\n\n   $$\n   \\text{MARE} = \\max(\\frac{\\text{abs}(actual - golden)}{\\text{abs}(golden)+\\text{1e-7}})\n   $$\n\n**通过标准**：\n\n| 数据类型 | FLOAT16 | BFLOAT16 | FLOAT32 | HiFLOAT32 | FLOAT8 E4M3 | FLOAT8 E5M2 |\n|----------|---------|----------|---------|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| **通过阈值(Threshold)** | 2^-10 | 2^-7 | 2^-13 | 2^-11 | 2^-3 | 2^-2 |\n\n当平均相对误差 MERE < Threshold，最大相对误差 MARE < 10 * Threshold 时判定为通过。\n\n\n## 5. 标准 Golden 代码\n\n```python\nimport torch\n\ndef sigmoid(\n    x: torch.Tensor\n) -> torch.Tensor:\n    \"\"\"\n    对输入Tensor完成Sigmoid运算\n\n    公式: y = 1 / (1 + e^(-x))\n\n    Args:\n        x: 输入张量\n\n    Returns:\n        输出张量，Sigmoid激活结果\n    \"\"\"\n\n    y = torch.sigmoid(x)\n    return y\n```\n\n## 6. 额外信息\n\n### 算子调用示例\n\n```python\nimport torch\nimport cann_bench\n\nx = torch.randn(1024, 1024, dtype=torch.float32, device=\"npu\")\ny = cann_bench.sigmoid(x)\n```\n",
+    "reference/native-template.py": "\"\"\"Small six-source native acceptance fixture; FP32 contiguous vector addition.\"\"\"\nimport json\nproject_json_src = json.dumps([{\n    'op': 'AuditAddCustom', 'language': 'cpp',\n    'input_desc': [{'name': name, 'param_type': 'required', 'format': ['ND'], 'type': ['float']} for name in ('x', 'y')],\n    'output_desc': [{'name': 'z', 'param_type': 'required', 'format': ['ND'], 'type': ['float']}],\n}])\nhost_tiling_src = r'''\n#ifndef AUDIT_ADD_CUSTOM_TILING_H\n#define AUDIT_ADD_CUSTOM_TILING_H\n#include <cstdint>\nstruct AuditAddCustomTilingData { uint32_t size; };\n#endif\n'''\nhost_operator_src = r'''\n#include \"../op_kernel/audit_add_custom_tiling.h\"\n#include \"register/op_def_registry.h\"\nnamespace optiling {\nstatic ge::graphStatus TilingFunc(gert::TilingContext* c) {\n auto* t = c->GetTilingData<AuditAddCustomTilingData>();\n t->size = c->GetInputShape(0)->GetStorageShape().GetShapeSize();\n c->SetBlockDim(1); c->GetWorkspaceSizes(1)[0] = 0; return ge::GRAPH_SUCCESS;\n}}\nnamespace ge {\nstatic ge::graphStatus InferShape(gert::InferShapeContext* c) {\n *c->GetOutputShape(0) = *c->GetInputShape(0); return GRAPH_SUCCESS;\n}\nstatic ge::graphStatus InferDataType(gert::InferDataTypeContext* c) {\n c->SetOutputDataType(0, c->GetInputDataType(0)); return GRAPH_SUCCESS;\n}}\nnamespace ops {\nclass AuditAddCustom: public OpDef {\npublic: explicit AuditAddCustom(const char* name): OpDef(name) {\n this->Input(\"x\").ParamType(REQUIRED).DataType({ge::DT_FLOAT}).Format({ge::FORMAT_ND}).UnknownShapeFormat({ge::FORMAT_ND});\n this->Input(\"y\").ParamType(REQUIRED).DataType({ge::DT_FLOAT}).Format({ge::FORMAT_ND}).UnknownShapeFormat({ge::FORMAT_ND});\n this->Output(\"z\").ParamType(REQUIRED).DataType({ge::DT_FLOAT}).Format({ge::FORMAT_ND}).UnknownShapeFormat({ge::FORMAT_ND});\n this->SetInferShape(ge::InferShape).SetInferDataType(ge::InferDataType);\n this->AICore().SetTiling(optiling::TilingFunc); this->AICore().AddConfig(\"ascend910_93\");\n}};\nOP_ADD(AuditAddCustom);\n}\n'''\nkernel_src = r'''\n#include \"kernel_operator.h\"\n#include \"audit_add_custom_tiling.h\"\nextern \"C\" __global__ __aicore__ void audit_add_custom(GM_ADDR x, GM_ADDR y, GM_ADDR z, GM_ADDR workspace, GM_ADDR tiling) {\n REGISTER_TILING_DEFAULT(AuditAddCustomTilingData);\n GET_TILING_DATA(t, tiling);\n AscendC::GlobalTensor<float> a,b,c;\n a.SetGlobalBuffer((__gm__ float*)x, t.size);\n b.SetGlobalBuffer((__gm__ float*)y, t.size);\n c.SetGlobalBuffer((__gm__ float*)z, t.size);\n for(uint32_t i=0;i<t.size;++i) c.SetValue(i,a.GetValue(i)+b.GetValue(i));\n}\n'''\npython_bind_src = r'''\n#include <torch/extension.h>\n#include \"pytorch_npu_helper.hpp\"\nat::Tensor add(const at::Tensor& x, const at::Tensor& y) {\n auto z=at::empty_like(x); EXEC_NPU_CMD(aclnnAuditAddCustom, x, y, z); return z;\n}\nPYBIND11_MODULE(TORCH_EXTENSION_NAME, m) { m.def(\"add\", &add); }\n'''\nmodel_src = '''\nimport torch\nimport custom_ops_lib\nclass ModelNew(torch.nn.Module):\n    def forward(self, x, y): return custom_ops_lib.add(x, y)\n'''\n",
+    "reference/verified-vector.py": "\"\"\"Six-source Ascend C candidate: fp32 vector addition c = a + b using the Vector unit.\"\"\"\nimport json\n\nproject_json_src = json.dumps([{\n    'op': 'VectorAddCustom', 'language': 'cpp',\n    'input_desc': [{'name': name, 'param_type': 'required', 'format': ['ND'], 'type': ['float']} for name in ('x', 'y')],\n    'output_desc': [{'name': 'z', 'param_type': 'required', 'format': ['ND'], 'type': ['float']}],\n}])\n\nhost_tiling_src = r'''\n#ifndef VECTOR_ADD_CUSTOM_TILING_H\n#define VECTOR_ADD_CUSTOM_TILING_H\n#include <cstdint>\nstruct VectorAddCustomTilingData {\n    uint32_t size;     // total element count\n    uint32_t tileLen;  // elements handled per UB tile (32B aligned)\n    uint32_t tileNum;  // number of tiles\n    uint32_t lastLen;  // elements in the last tile\n};\n#endif\n'''\n\nhost_operator_src = r'''\n#include \"../op_kernel/vector_add_custom_tiling.h\"\n#include \"register/op_def_registry.h\"\n\nnamespace optiling {\nstatic ge::graphStatus TilingFunc(gert::TilingContext* c) {\n    auto* t = c->GetTilingData<VectorAddCustomTilingData>();\n    uint32_t size = static_cast<uint32_t>(c->GetInputShape(0)->GetStorageShape().GetShapeSize());\n    constexpr uint32_t kAlign = 8;  // 32B / sizeof(float)\n    uint32_t tileLen = 8192;\n    if (tileLen > size) tileLen = size;\n    tileLen = (tileLen / kAlign) * kAlign;\n    if (tileLen == 0) tileLen = kAlign;\n    if (tileLen > size) tileLen = size;\n    uint32_t tileNum = (size + tileLen - 1) / tileLen;\n    if (tileNum == 0) { tileLen = kAlign; tileNum = 1; }\n    t->size = size;\n    t->tileLen = tileLen;\n    t->tileNum = tileNum;\n    t->lastLen = size - (tileNum - 1) * tileLen;\n    c->SetBlockDim(1);\n    c->GetWorkspaceSizes(1)[0] = 0;\n    return ge::GRAPH_SUCCESS;\n}\n}\n\nnamespace ge {\nstatic ge::graphStatus InferShape(gert::InferShapeContext* c) {\n    *c->GetOutputShape(0) = *c->GetInputShape(0);\n    return GRAPH_SUCCESS;\n}\nstatic ge::graphStatus InferDataType(gert::InferDataTypeContext* c) {\n    c->SetOutputDataType(0, c->GetInputDataType(0));\n    return GRAPH_SUCCESS;\n}\n}\n\nnamespace ops {\nclass VectorAddCustom : public OpDef {\npublic:\n    explicit VectorAddCustom(const char* name) : OpDef(name) {\n        this->Input(\"x\").ParamType(REQUIRED).DataType({ge::DT_FLOAT}).Format({ge::FORMAT_ND}).UnknownShapeFormat({ge::FORMAT_ND});\n        this->Input(\"y\").ParamType(REQUIRED).DataType({ge::DT_FLOAT}).Format({ge::FORMAT_ND}).UnknownShapeFormat({ge::FORMAT_ND});\n        this->Output(\"z\").ParamType(REQUIRED).DataType({ge::DT_FLOAT}).Format({ge::FORMAT_ND}).UnknownShapeFormat({ge::FORMAT_ND});\n        this->SetInferShape(ge::InferShape).SetInferDataType(ge::InferDataType);\n        this->AICore().SetTiling(optiling::TilingFunc);\n        this->AICore().AddConfig(\"ascend910_93\");\n    }\n};\nOP_ADD(VectorAddCustom);\n}\n'''\n\nkernel_src = r'''\n#include \"kernel_operator.h\"\n#include \"vector_add_custom_tiling.h\"\n\nusing namespace AscendC;\n\nclass VectorAddKernel {\npublic:\n    __aicore__ inline VectorAddKernel() {}\n\n    __aicore__ inline void Init(GM_ADDR x, GM_ADDR y, GM_ADDR z, const VectorAddCustomTilingData& t) {\n        xGm_.SetGlobalBuffer((__gm__ float*)x, t.size);\n        yGm_.SetGlobalBuffer((__gm__ float*)y, t.size);\n        zGm_.SetGlobalBuffer((__gm__ float*)z, t.size);\n        pipe_.InitBuffer(inQx_, 1, t.tileLen * sizeof(float));\n        pipe_.InitBuffer(inQy_, 1, t.tileLen * sizeof(float));\n        pipe_.InitBuffer(outQ_, 1, t.tileLen * sizeof(float));\n        size_ = t.size;\n        tileLen_ = t.tileLen;\n    }\n\n    __aicore__ inline void Process() {\n        uint32_t off = 0;\n        while (off < size_) {\n            uint32_t n = size_ - off;\n            if (n > tileLen_) n = tileLen_;\n            CopyAdd(off, n);\n            off += n;\n        }\n    }\n\nprivate:\n    __aicore__ inline void CopyAdd(uint32_t srcOff, uint32_t n) {\n        LocalTensor<float> lx = inQx_.AllocTensor<float>();\n        LocalTensor<float> ly = inQy_.AllocTensor<float>();\n        LocalTensor<float> lz = outQ_.AllocTensor<float>();\n        const uint32_t aligned = n & ~7u;\n        const uint32_t tail = n - aligned;\n        if (aligned > 0) {\n            DataCopy(lx, xGm_[srcOff], aligned);\n            DataCopy(ly, yGm_[srcOff], aligned);\n        }\n        if (tail > 0) {\n            DataCopyExtParams tp{1, static_cast<uint32_t>(tail * sizeof(float)), 0, 0, 0};\n            DataCopyPadExtParams<float> padParams{false, 0, 0, 0.0f};\n            DataCopyPad(lx[aligned], xGm_[srcOff + aligned], tp, padParams);\n            DataCopyPad(ly[aligned], yGm_[srcOff + aligned], tp, padParams);\n        }\n        inQx_.EnQue(lx);\n        inQy_.EnQue(ly);\n        lx = inQx_.DeQue<float>();\n        ly = inQy_.DeQue<float>();\n        Add(lz, lx, ly, n);\n        outQ_.EnQue(lz);\n        lz = outQ_.DeQue<float>();\n        if (aligned > 0) {\n            DataCopy(zGm_[srcOff], lz, aligned);\n        }\n        if (tail > 0) {\n            DataCopyExtParams tp{1, static_cast<uint32_t>(tail * sizeof(float)), 0, 0, 0};\n            DataCopyPad(zGm_[srcOff + aligned], lz[aligned], tp);\n        }\n        inQx_.FreeTensor(lx);\n        inQy_.FreeTensor(ly);\n        outQ_.FreeTensor(lz);\n    }\n\n    TPipe pipe_;\n    TQue<QuePosition::VECIN, 1> inQx_;\n    TQue<QuePosition::VECIN, 1> inQy_;\n    TQue<QuePosition::VECOUT, 1> outQ_;\n    GlobalTensor<float> xGm_, yGm_, zGm_;\n    uint32_t size_ = 0;\n    uint32_t tileLen_ = 0;\n};\n\nextern \"C\" __global__ __aicore__ void vector_add_custom(GM_ADDR x, GM_ADDR y, GM_ADDR z, GM_ADDR workspace, GM_ADDR tiling) {\n    REGISTER_TILING_DEFAULT(VectorAddCustomTilingData);\n    GET_TILING_DATA(t, tiling);\n    VectorAddKernel k;\n    k.Init(x, y, z, t);\n    k.Process();\n}\n'''\n\npython_bind_src = r'''\n#include <torch/extension.h>\n#include \"pytorch_npu_helper.hpp\"\nat::Tensor add(const at::Tensor& x, const at::Tensor& y) {\n    auto z = at::empty_like(x);\n    EXEC_NPU_CMD(aclnnVectorAddCustom, x, y, z);\n    return z;\n}\nPYBIND11_MODULE(custom_ops_lib, m) { m.def(\"add\", &add); }\n'''\n\nmodel_src = '''\nimport torch\nimport custom_ops_lib\n\nclass ModelNew(torch.nn.Module):\n    def forward(self, x, y):\n        return custom_ops_lib.add(x, y)\n'''\n",
+    "reference/qualified-native.py": "\"\"\"Conservative one-core native seed for a separately labelled optimization trial.\n\nHand-authored from the verified Vector queue pattern. It is not a model-generated\nsolution or a performance claim; the full CANNBench suite must qualify it first.\n\"\"\"\nimport json\n\nproject_json_src = json.dumps([{\n    'op': 'SigmoidCustom', 'language': 'cpp',\n    'input_desc': [{'name': 'x', 'param_type': 'required', 'format': ['ND'],\n                    'type': ['float16', 'float', 'bfloat16']}],\n    'output_desc': [{'name': 'y', 'param_type': 'required', 'format': ['ND'],\n                     'type': ['float16', 'float', 'bfloat16']}],\n}])\n\nhost_tiling_src = r'''\n#ifndef SIGMOID_CUSTOM_TILING_H\n#define SIGMOID_CUSTOM_TILING_H\n#include <cstdint>\nstruct SigmoidCustomTilingData { uint32_t total; uint32_t perCore; uint32_t tile; };\n#endif\n'''\n\nhost_operator_src = r'''\n#include \"../op_kernel/sigmoid_custom_tiling.h\"\n#include \"register/op_def_registry.h\"\nnamespace optiling {\nstatic ge::graphStatus TilingFunc(gert::TilingContext* c) {\n    auto* t = c->GetTilingData<SigmoidCustomTilingData>();\n    t->total = static_cast<uint32_t>(c->GetInputShape(0)->GetStorageShape().GetShapeSize());\n    constexpr uint32_t cores = 1;\n    t->perCore = ((t->total + cores - 1) / cores + 15) / 16 * 16;\n    t->tile = 2048;\n    c->SetBlockDim(cores);\n    c->GetWorkspaceSizes(1)[0] = 0;\n    return ge::GRAPH_SUCCESS;\n}\n}\nnamespace ge {\nstatic ge::graphStatus InferShape(gert::InferShapeContext* c) {\n    *c->GetOutputShape(0) = *c->GetInputShape(0); return GRAPH_SUCCESS;\n}\nstatic ge::graphStatus InferDataType(gert::InferDataTypeContext* c) {\n    c->SetOutputDataType(0, c->GetInputDataType(0)); return GRAPH_SUCCESS;\n}\n}\nnamespace ops {\nclass SigmoidCustom : public OpDef {\npublic:\n    explicit SigmoidCustom(const char* name) : OpDef(name) {\n        this->Input(\"x\").ParamType(REQUIRED).DataType({ge::DT_FLOAT16,ge::DT_FLOAT,ge::DT_BF16})\n            .Format({ge::FORMAT_ND,ge::FORMAT_ND,ge::FORMAT_ND})\n            .UnknownShapeFormat({ge::FORMAT_ND,ge::FORMAT_ND,ge::FORMAT_ND});\n        this->Output(\"y\").ParamType(REQUIRED).DataType({ge::DT_FLOAT16,ge::DT_FLOAT,ge::DT_BF16})\n            .Format({ge::FORMAT_ND,ge::FORMAT_ND,ge::FORMAT_ND})\n            .UnknownShapeFormat({ge::FORMAT_ND,ge::FORMAT_ND,ge::FORMAT_ND});\n        this->SetInferShape(ge::InferShape).SetInferDataType(ge::InferDataType);\n        this->AICore().SetTiling(optiling::TilingFunc).AddConfig(\"ascend910_93\");\n    }\n};\nOP_ADD(SigmoidCustom);\n}\n'''\n\nkernel_src = r'''\n#include \"kernel_operator.h\"\n#include \"sigmoid_custom_tiling.h\"\nusing namespace AscendC;\ntemplate<class T> class SigmoidKernel {\npublic:\n    __aicore__ inline void Init(GM_ADDR x, GM_ADDR y, const SigmoidCustomTilingData& t) {\n        uint32_t base = GetBlockIdx() * t.perCore;\n        count = base < t.total ? (t.perCore < t.total - base ? t.perCore : t.total - base) : 0;\n        tile = t.tile;\n        xGm.SetGlobalBuffer((__gm__ T*)x + base, count);\n        yGm.SetGlobalBuffer((__gm__ T*)y + base, count);\n        pipe.InitBuffer(input, 1, tile * sizeof(T));\n        pipe.InitBuffer(output, 1, tile * sizeof(T));\n        pipe.InitBuffer(scratch, tile * sizeof(float));\n        pipe.InitBuffer(onesBuffer, tile * sizeof(float));\n    }\n    __aicore__ inline void Process() {\n        for (uint32_t off = 0; off < count; off += tile) {\n            uint32_t n = tile < count - off ? tile : count - off;\n            LocalTensor<T> x = input.AllocTensor<T>();\n            DataCopyExtParams cp{1, static_cast<uint32_t>(n * sizeof(T)), 0, 0, 0};\n            DataCopyPadExtParams<T> pad{false, 0, 0, 0};\n            DataCopyPad(x, xGm[off], cp, pad);\n            input.EnQue(x); x = input.DeQue<T>();\n            LocalTensor<float> f = scratch.Get<float>();\n            if constexpr (sizeof(T) == sizeof(float)) {\n                Muls(f, x.template ReinterpretCast<float>(), -1.0f, n);\n            } else {\n                Cast(f, x, RoundMode::CAST_NONE, n);\n                PipeBarrier<PIPE_V>(); Muls(f, f, -1.0f, n);\n            }\n            PipeBarrier<PIPE_V>(); Exp(f, f, n);\n            PipeBarrier<PIPE_V>(); Adds(f, f, 1.0f, n);\n            LocalTensor<float> ones = onesBuffer.Get<float>();\n            PipeBarrier<PIPE_V>(); Duplicate(ones, 1.0f, n);\n            PipeBarrier<PIPE_V>(); Div(f, ones, f, n);\n            PipeBarrier<PIPE_V>();\n            LocalTensor<T> y = output.AllocTensor<T>();\n            if constexpr (sizeof(T) == sizeof(float)) {\n                Muls(y.template ReinterpretCast<float>(), f, 1.0f, n);\n            } else { Cast(y, f, RoundMode::CAST_RINT, n); }\n            output.EnQue(y); y = output.DeQue<T>();\n            DataCopyPad(yGm[off], y, cp);\n            input.FreeTensor(x); output.FreeTensor(y);\n        }\n    }\nprivate:\n    TPipe pipe;\n    TQue<QuePosition::VECIN,1> input;\n    TQue<QuePosition::VECOUT,1> output;\n    TBuf<TPosition::VECCALC> scratch;\n    TBuf<TPosition::VECCALC> onesBuffer;\n    GlobalTensor<T> xGm, yGm;\n    uint32_t count, tile;\n};\nextern \"C\" __global__ __aicore__ void sigmoid_custom(GM_ADDR x, GM_ADDR y, GM_ADDR workspace, GM_ADDR tiling) {\n    REGISTER_TILING_DEFAULT(SigmoidCustomTilingData);\n    GET_TILING_DATA(t, tiling);\n    SigmoidKernel<DTYPE_X> kernel;\n    kernel.Init(x, y, t); kernel.Process();\n}\n'''\n\npython_bind_src = r'''\n#include <torch/extension.h>\n#include \"pytorch_npu_helper.hpp\"\nat::Tensor sigmoid(const at::Tensor& x) {\n    auto y = at::empty_like(x); EXEC_NPU_CMD(aclnnSigmoidCustom, x, y); return y;\n}\nPYBIND11_MODULE(TORCH_EXTENSION_NAME, m) { m.def(\"sigmoid\", &sigmoid); }\n'''\n\nmodel_src = '''\nimport torch\nimport custom_ops_lib\nclass ModelNew(torch.nn.Module):\n    def forward(self, x): return custom_ops_lib.sigmoid(x)\n'''\n"
+  },
+  "contract": {
+    "suite": "CANNBench Season 1 Sigmoid, 20 cases",
+    "turns": 40
+  }
+}
diff --git a/examples/cann/task_bundle.py b/examples/cann/task_bundle.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ae37a30
--- /dev/null
+++ b/examples/cann/task_bundle.py
@@ -0,0 +1,83 @@
+"""Compile editable CANN inputs without importing candidate code or starting effects."""
+from pathlib import Path
+import argparse
+import ast
+import hashlib
+import json
+import math
+
+from make_tasks import build_task, FIELDS
+
+
+def read_local(root, name):
+    if not isinstance(name, str) or Path(name).name != name or name in ('', '.', '..'):
+        raise ValueError('task references must be simple filenames inside the task directory')
+    path = root / name
+    if path.is_symlink() or not path.is_file() or path.stat().st_size > 1024 * 1024:
+        raise ValueError('task input must be a bounded regular file: ' + name)
+    return path.read_text(encoding='utf8')
+
+
+def validate_case(case):
+    common = {'kind', 'task_id', 'native_operator', 'soc', 'device', 'dtype', 'seeds',
+              'distribution', 'atol', 'rtol'}
+    extra = {'shape'} if case.get('kind') == 'vector_add' else {'m', 'n', 'k', 'accumulator_dtype'}
+    if set(case) != common | extra:
+        raise ValueError('case contains missing or unsupported fields')
+    expected = {'vector_add': ('vector_add', 'float32'), 'matmul': ('matmul', 'float16')}
+    if case['kind'] not in expected or (case['native_operator'], case['dtype']) != expected[case['kind']]:
+        raise ValueError('these baselines support FP32 vector_add and FP16 matmul only')
+    if case['kind'] == 'matmul' and case['accumulator_dtype'] != 'float32':
+        raise ValueError('Cube baseline requires FP32 accumulation')
+    if type(case['device']) is not int or case['device'] < 0:
+        raise ValueError('device must be a nonnegative integer')
+    for name in ('atol', 'rtol'):
+        if type(case[name]) not in (int, float) or not math.isfinite(case[name]) or case[name] < 0:
+            raise ValueError(name + ' must be finite and nonnegative')
+    if len(set(case['seeds'])) != 5:
+        raise ValueError('five distinct correctness seeds are required')
+    if not isinstance(case['task_id'], str) or not case['task_id'].strip():
+        raise ValueError('task_id is required')
+    if not isinstance(case['soc'], str) or not case['soc'].startswith('ai_core-Ascend'):
+        raise ValueError('an explicit Ascend target is required')
+
+
+def load_bundle(path, mode='generate'):
+    path = Path(path).absolute()
+    author_text = read_local(path.parent, path.name)
+    author = json.loads(author_text)
+    if set(author) != {'schema_version', 'goal', 'case_file', 'baseline_file'}:
+        raise ValueError('expected the CANN authoring task schema; use task.compiled.json with runTask directly')
+    if author['schema_version'] != 'kernelbridge.cann-task/v1':
+        raise ValueError('unsupported CANN task schema')
+    if not isinstance(author['goal'], str) or not 1 <= len(author['goal'].strip()) <= 8000:
+        raise ValueError('goal must contain 1..8000 characters')
+    case_text = read_local(path.parent, author['case_file'])
+    baseline = read_local(path.parent, author['baseline_file'])
+    case = json.loads(case_text)
+    validate_case(case)
+    tree = ast.parse(baseline)
+    names = {target.id for statement in tree.body if isinstance(statement, ast.Assign)
+             for target in statement.targets if isinstance(target, ast.Name)}
+    if not set(FIELDS) <= names:
+        raise ValueError('baseline must define the six native source fields')
+    task, reference, request = build_task(case, baseline, author['goal'], mode)
+    inputs = {path.name: author_text, author['case_file']: case_text, author['baseline_file']: baseline}
+    manifest = {'schema_version': 'kernelbridge.cann-inputs/v1', 'mode': mode,
+                'source_directory': str(path.parent), 'inputs': {
+                    name: {'sha256': hashlib.sha256(text.encode()).hexdigest(), 'bytes': len(text.encode())}
+                    for name, text in inputs.items()}}
+    return task, reference, request, manifest
+
+
+def main():
+    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)
+    parser.add_argument('--task', type=Path, required=True)
+    parser.add_argument('--mode', choices=['generate', 'optimize'], default='generate')
+    args = parser.parse_args()
+    task, reference, request, manifest = load_bundle(args.task, args.mode)
+    print(json.dumps({'task': task, 'reference': reference, 'request': request, 'manifest': manifest}, ensure_ascii=False))
+
+
+if __name__ == '__main__':
+    main()
diff --git a/examples/cann/tools/README.md b/examples/cann/tools/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e6a770f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/examples/cann/tools/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+# 通用算子诊断工具
+
+Pi 负责模型与工具回合，LoopX 提供可选 Goal 调度。工具通过 KernelBridge 的 `business_tools` 注册，配置明确命令、参数合同、源码哈希、预算与超时。CPU、GPU、NPU 采集器均可使用这个接口；`examples/cann` 提供 Ascend 的配置示例。
+
+| 类别 | Pi 工具 | 产物 |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| 采集 | `ir_collect` | 当前候选的设备 LLVM、编译日志、源码与编译器身份 |
+| 采集 | `profiler_collect` | 正确性检查、NPU timeline、PipeUtilization、原始 CSV |
+| 解析 | `diagnostics_parse` | LLVM 函数与调用统计、profiler CSV 字段及记录 |
+| 展示 | `diagnostics_render` | 复用 PyPTO 的 LLVM 对照 HTML |
+| 读取 | `diagnostics_read` | collection 文件清单、哈希、分页文本 |
+
+在 CANN profile 中设置 `"diagnostics": true` 即可暴露这些工具。`false` 或省略该字段使用当前任务配置的基础工具与评测工具。`config.business_tools` 接入其他平台的命令适配器；适配器从 stdin 读取 Action，stdout 返回 `{"status":"completed","data":{...}}`，原始标准输出、错误输出和 Outcome 写入执行账本对应目录。
+
+采集输出位于 `evaluations/diagnostics/<collection>/`；工具调用回执位于 `state/business-tools/<tool>/`。解析与展示引用采集返回的 collection 和相对路径，按清单哈希读取。采集使用独立构建目录，性能验收使用任务配置的配对计时协议。
+
+`ir_bridge.py`、`trace_lab.py` 与 `vendor/pypto` 复用现有 IR/trace 展示代码；上游版本及逐文件哈希在 `vendor/pypto/provenance.json`，许可证随目录保留。LLVM 展示比较显式选定的文本快照。Trace 清洗保留原始采集，按 core 和 PC 对照指令统计。
+
+部署采集器配置本机编译器、驱动、CANN 和 `torch_npu`。远端部署可配置直接 SSH 的 `host`、`user`、`port` 与 `identity`，或使用自有的业务工具适配器。
diff --git a/examples/cann/tools/diagnostics.py b/examples/cann/tools/diagnostics.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9e86571
--- /dev/null
+++ b/examples/cann/tools/diagnostics.py
@@ -0,0 +1,211 @@
+"""Local operator diagnostics: collection, parsing, bounded reads and IR rendering."""
+import csv
+import hashlib
+import json
+import os
+from pathlib import Path
+import re
+import shlex
+import shutil
+import subprocess
+import sys
+from functools import partial
+
+
+def sha(data):
+    return hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest()
+
+
+def inventory(root):
+    files = []
+    for path in sorted(root.rglob('*')):
+        if path.is_symlink():
+            continue
+        if path.is_file() and path.name != 'manifest.json':
+            files.append({'path': path.relative_to(root).as_posix(), 'bytes': path.stat().st_size,
+                          'sha256': sha(path.read_bytes())})
+    return files
+
+
+def artifact(root, collection, name=None):
+    if not re.fullmatch(r'[a-f0-9]{64}', collection):
+        raise ValueError('Expected a collection identity returned by a diagnostic tool')
+    folder = root / collection
+    if folder.resolve() != folder:
+        raise ValueError('Diagnostic storage cannot traverse links')
+    manifest = json.loads((folder / 'manifest.json').read_text())
+    if name is None:
+        return manifest
+    path = folder / name
+    row = next((row for row in manifest['files'] if row['path'] == name), None)
+    if not row or path.resolve() != path or not path.is_relative_to(folder) or '..' in Path(name).parts:
+        raise ValueError('Artifact is not in this collection')
+    if path.stat().st_size > 128 * 1024 * 1024:
+        raise ValueError('Artifact exceeds diagnostic read limit')
+    if sha(path.read_bytes()) != row['sha256']:
+        raise ValueError('Diagnostic artifact digest changed')
+    return path
+
+
+def emit_device_bitcode(build, output, compiler):
+    """Replay retained device compilation with the same source, defines and target."""
+    records = []
+    seen = set()
+    for log in sorted(build.rglob('*.log')):
+        for line in log.read_text(errors='replace').splitlines():
+            if not line.startswith('/') or 'bisheng ' not in line:
+                continue
+            argv = shlex.split(line)
+            if Path(argv[0]).resolve() != Path(compiler).resolve() or '-c' not in argv or '-E' in argv:
+                continue
+            if not any(arg.startswith('--cce-aicore-arch=') for arg in argv) or '-D__GET_CODE_CHANNEL__' in argv:
+                continue
+            sources = [Path(arg) for arg in argv if arg.endswith(('.cpp', '.cce'))]
+            if not sources or any(not p.resolve().is_relative_to(build.resolve()) for p in sources):
+                continue
+            key = tuple(argv)
+            if key in seen:
+                continue
+            seen.add(key)
+            directory = output / str(len(records)); directory.mkdir(parents=True)
+            command = []; index = 0
+            while index < len(argv):
+                arg = argv[index]; index += 1
+                if arg in ('-o', '-MF', '-MT'):
+                    index += 1
+                elif arg not in ('-MD', '-MMD', '-save-temps'):
+                    command.append(arg)
+            command += ['-emit-llvm', '-o', str(directory / 'kernel.bc')]
+            with (directory / 'compile.log').open('w') as stream:
+                process = subprocess.run(command, cwd=directory, stdout=stream, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, timeout=180)
+            record = {'original_command': argv, 'command': command, 'returncode': process.returncode,
+                      'sources': [{'path': str(p.relative_to(build)), 'sha256': sha(p.read_bytes())} for p in sources]}
+            records.append(record)
+    (output / 'commands.json').write_text(json.dumps(records, indent=2) + '\n')
+    return list(output.rglob('*.bc'))
+
+
+def collect(config, root, kind):
+    from kernelcat_executor.build.inputs import BuildSettings
+    from kernelcat_executor.backends.ascend.compiler import compile_sources
+    from kernelcat_executor.evaluation.protocols.six_source.session import AscendBackend
+    from kernelcat_executor.evaluation.protocols.six_source.config import BACKEND_ROOT
+    source = Path.cwd() / 'solution.py'
+    if source.resolve() != source or not source.is_file() or source.stat().st_size > 4_000_000:
+        raise ValueError('Expected the admitted solution.py')
+    candidate = source.read_bytes()
+    (root / 'solution.py').write_bytes(candidate)
+    build = root / 'build'; build.mkdir()
+    shutil.copytree(BACKEND_ROOT / 'templates/CppExtension', build / 'CppExtension')
+    settings = BuildSettings(config['operator'], build, config['soc'], config['device'])
+    os.environ.update(ASCEND_DEVICE_ID=str(config['device']), ASCENDC_DEVICE=config['soc'],
+                      OP_ENGINEER_DIR=str(build), PYTHON=sys.executable)
+    compiler = partial(compile_sources, diagnostic_options=('-save-temps', '--save-temp-files') if kind == 'ir' else ())
+    backend = AscendBackend(settings, compiler=compiler, atol=config['atol'], rtol=config['rtol'])
+    try:
+        ok, error = backend.compile(candidate.decode())
+        if not ok:
+            raise RuntimeError(error)
+        result = {'candidate_sha256': sha(candidate), 'build': backend.build_manifest, 'kind': kind,
+                  'device': config['device'], 'soc': config['soc']}
+        if kind == 'ir':
+            compiler_path = shutil.which('bisheng')
+            if not compiler_path:
+                home = Path(os.environ.get('ASCEND_HOME_PATH', '/usr/local/Ascend/ascend-toolkit/latest'))
+                matches = sorted(home.glob('**/bin/bisheng'))
+                compiler_path = str(matches[0]) if matches else None
+            if not compiler_path:
+                raise ValueError('bisheng is required for LLVM decoding')
+            result['compiler_sha256'] = sha(Path(compiler_path).read_bytes())
+            result['compiler_version'] = subprocess.check_output([compiler_path, '--version'], text=True, timeout=20)
+            bitcode = list(build.rglob('*.bc'))
+            decoded = root / 'llvm'; decoded.mkdir()
+            if not bitcode:
+                bitcode = emit_device_bitcode(build, decoded, compiler_path)
+            for index, path in enumerate(bitcode):
+                target = decoded / (str(index) + '-' + path.stem + '.ll')
+                command = [compiler_path, '-cc1', '-x', 'ir', '-emit-llvm', '-triple', 'hiipu64-hisilicon-cce', '-o', str(target), str(path)]
+                with (decoded / (target.stem + '.log')).open('w') as log:
+                    process = subprocess.run(command, stdout=log, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, timeout=120)
+                if process.returncode:
+                    target.unlink(missing_ok=True)
+            result['llvm_files'] = [str(path.relative_to(root)) for path in decoded.glob('*.ll')]
+            if not result['llvm_files']:
+                raise ValueError('Compiler retained no decodable device bitcode; inspect build logs')
+        else:
+            import torch
+            import torch_npu
+            from kernelcat_executor.evaluation.protocols.six_source.correctness import _to_device
+            reference = Path(config['reference']).read_text()
+            correct, info, stage = backend.correctness(reference)
+            result.update(correctness=correct, correctness_info=info, failure_stage=stage)
+            if not correct:
+                raise ValueError('Diagnostic candidate failed correctness: ' + str(info))
+            context = backend.context
+            model = context['ModelNew'](*_to_device(context['get_init_inputs'](), backend.runtime.device)).to(backend.runtime.device)
+            inputs = _to_device(context['get_inputs'](), backend.runtime.device)
+            with torch.no_grad():
+                for _ in range(3): model(*inputs)
+                torch_npu.npu.synchronize()
+                experimental = torch_npu.profiler._ExperimentalConfig(
+                    profiler_level=torch_npu.profiler.ProfilerLevel.Level1,
+                    aic_metrics=torch_npu.profiler.AiCMetrics.PipeUtilization)
+                with torch_npu.profiler.profile(activities=[torch_npu.profiler.ProfilerActivity.NPU],
+                    on_trace_ready=torch_npu.profiler.tensorboard_trace_handler(str(root / 'profile')),
+                    record_shapes=False, with_stack=False, profile_memory=False, experimental_config=experimental):
+                    for _ in range(5):
+                        model(*inputs); torch_npu.npu.synchronize()
+            result.update(torch=torch.__version__, torch_npu=torch_npu.__version__,
+                          metric='PipeUtilization', warmup=3, repeats=5, measurement_kind='profiled_diagnostic')
+            if not list((root / 'profile').rglob('kernel_details.csv')):
+                raise ValueError('Profiler returned no kernel_details.csv')
+        return result
+    finally:
+        backend.close()
+
+
+def main(config):
+    action = json.load(sys.stdin); name = action['tool']; args = action['arguments']
+    root = Path(config['state']) / 'diagnostics'; root.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
+    if name == 'diagnostics_read':
+        item = artifact(root, args['collection'], args.get('path'))
+        if isinstance(item, dict):
+            return {'status': 'completed', 'data': item}
+        offset = args.get('offset', 0); limit = min(args.get('limit', 8192), 16384)
+        with item.open('rb') as stream:
+            stream.seek(offset); data = stream.read(limit)
+        return {'status': 'completed', 'data': {'text': data.decode('utf-8', errors='replace'),
+                'offset': offset, 'next_offset': offset + len(data), 'bytes': item.stat().st_size}}
+    identity = sha(action['id'].encode()); output = root / identity; output.mkdir()
+    try:
+        if name in ('ir_collect', 'profiler_collect'):
+            # Native/compiler output is retained separately from the finite JSON reply.
+            with (output / 'collector.log').open('w') as log:
+                original = os.dup(1); os.dup2(log.fileno(), 1)
+                try: report = collect(config, output, 'ir' if name == 'ir_collect' else 'profiler')
+                finally: sys.stdout.flush(); os.dup2(original, 1); os.close(original)
+        elif name == 'diagnostics_parse':
+            path = artifact(root, args['collection'], args['path'])
+            if path.suffix == '.ll':
+                from ir_bridge import llvm_stats
+                report = {'kind': 'llvm', **llvm_stats(path.read_text()), 'source_sha256': sha(path.read_bytes())}
+            elif path.suffix == '.csv':
+                with path.open(newline='') as stream: rows = list(csv.DictReader(stream))
+                report = {'kind': 'profiler_csv', 'row_count': len(rows), 'columns': list(rows[0]) if rows else [],
+                          'rows': rows[:32], 'source_sha256': sha(path.read_bytes()), 'measurement_kind': 'profiled_diagnostic'}
+            else:
+                raise ValueError('Select a .ll or profiler .csv artifact')
+        elif name == 'diagnostics_render':
+            from ir_bridge import render_ir
+            paths = [artifact(root, args[prefix + '_collection'], args[prefix + '_path']) for prefix in ('before', 'after')]
+            report = render_ir(paths, output / 'ir.html', 'llvm')
+        else:
+            raise ValueError('Unknown diagnostic operation')
+        status = 'completed'
+    except Exception as error:
+        status = 'failed'; report = {'error': str(error)}
+    (output / 'report.json').write_text(json.dumps(report, indent=2) + '\n')
+    manifest = {'collection': identity, 'operation': name, 'status': status, 'report': report, 'files': inventory(output)}
+    (output / 'manifest.json').write_text(json.dumps(manifest, indent=2) + '\n')
+    return {'status': status, 'data': {'collection': identity, 'report': report,
+            'files': [row for row in manifest['files'] if not row['path'].startswith('build/')][:128]}}
diff --git a/examples/cann/tools/ir_bridge.py b/examples/cann/tools/ir_bridge.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..093f4ec
--- /dev/null
+++ b/examples/cann/tools/ir_bridge.py
@@ -0,0 +1,82 @@
+"""Reuse PyPTO's renderer, with an explicit text-only adapter for BiSheng LLVM."""
+import difflib
+from collections import Counter
+import html
+from pathlib import Path
+import re
+
+from trace_lab import fingerprint, save, verify_vendor
+
+
+def llvm_stats(text):
+    return dict(definitions=len(re.findall(r'^define ', text, re.M)),
+        debug_locations=len(re.findall(r'!DILocation\(', text)),
+        calls=dict(Counter(re.findall(r'\bcall\b[^\n]*?@([^ (]+)\(', text))))
+
+
+def select_llvm(text, pattern):
+    if not pattern:
+        return text
+    definitions = list(re.finditer(r'^define [^\n]*@([^ (]+)[^\n]*\{\n.*?^\}', text, re.M | re.S))
+    selected = [m for m in definitions if re.search(pattern, m[1])]
+    if not selected:
+        raise ValueError('no LLVM definition matches: ' + pattern)
+    return '\n\n'.join('; LLVM source line ' + str(text.count('\n', 0, m.start())+1) + '\n' + m[0]
+                       for m in selected)
+
+
+def render_ir(inputs, output, format, function=None):
+    revision = verify_vendor()
+    from vendor.pypto.ir_trace.html import render_html
+    from vendor.pypto.ir_trace.model import Snapshot, PassTrace, DiffSection, DiffHunk, DiffRow, split_source_lines
+    if format == 'pypto':
+        if len(inputs) != 1 or function:
+            raise ValueError('PyPTO requires one passes_dump directory')
+        from vendor.pypto.ir_trace.discovery import discover_snapshots
+        from vendor.pypto.ir_trace.diff import build_trace
+        snapshots = discover_snapshots(inputs[0])
+        traces = build_trace(snapshots, context=3)
+    else:
+        if len(inputs) < 2 or any(p.suffix != '.ll' for p in inputs):
+            raise ValueError('LLVM requires at least two .ll snapshots in explicit comparison order')
+        snapshots = []
+        for i, p in enumerate(inputs):
+            text = select_llvm(p.read_text(encoding='utf-8'), function)
+            snapshots.append(Snapshot(i, p.parent.name + '/' + p.name, p, text, split_source_lines(text),
+                'LLVM 文本对照：文件顺序不代表编译 Pass 顺序。无 PC 到源码映射。'
+                + (' 行号相对于筛选摘录；首行标明原 LLVM 文件行号。' if function else '')))
+        snapshots = tuple(snapshots)
+        traces = []
+        for i, (before, after) in enumerate(zip(snapshots, snapshots[1:]), 1):
+            # Plain text correspondence only: do not use Python AST/token matching for LLVM.
+            matcher = difflib.SequenceMatcher(None, before.lines, after.lines)
+            rows, inserted, deleted = [], 0, 0
+            for tag, a, b, c, d in matcher.get_opcodes():
+                inserted += d-c if tag != 'equal' else 0
+                deleted += b-a if tag != 'equal' else 0
+                for j in range(max(b-a, d-c)):
+                    left, right = a+j if a+j < b else None, c+j if c+j < d else None
+                    rows.append(DiffRow(tag, left+1 if left is not None else None,
+                        html.escape(before.lines[left]) if left is not None else '',
+                        right+1 if right is not None else None,
+                        html.escape(after.lines[right]) if right is not None else ''))
+            # Reuse only the vendor's presentation folding, independent of IR syntax.
+            from vendor.pypto.ir_trace.diff import _fold_rows
+            section = DiffSection(None, None, inserted, deleted, _fold_rows(tuple(rows), 3))
+            traces.append(PassTrace(i, after.pass_name, before, after, inserted, deleted, (section,)))
+        traces = tuple(traces)
+    output = Path(output)
+    if output.exists() or output.with_suffix('.json').exists():
+        raise ValueError('output already exists; use a new report name')
+    output.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
+    title = ('LLVM 文本对照（无 PC 映射）'
+             if format == 'llvm' else 'PyPTO Python IR pass dumps')
+    output.write_text(render_html(traces, source_name=title), encoding='utf-8')
+    evidence = dict(format=format, upstream_revision=revision, report=fingerprint(output),
+        inputs=[dict(fingerprint(s.path), statistics=llvm_stats(s.text) if format == 'llvm' else None)
+                for s in snapshots], pc_mapping='unavailable',
+        sequence='explicit_input_order' if format == 'llvm' else 'numbered_pypto_pass_dumps',
+        function_filter=function, displayed_lines='excerpt_relative' if function else 'physical_file_lines',
+        limitation='Static snapshot/text evidence only; not dynamic instruction counts or performance.')
+    save(output.with_suffix('.json'), evidence)
+    return dict(output=str(output.resolve()), format=format, snapshots=len(snapshots), pc_mapping='unavailable')
diff --git a/examples/cann/tools/trace_lab.py b/examples/cann/tools/trace_lab.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..eb9f983
--- /dev/null
+++ b/examples/cann/tools/trace_lab.py
@@ -0,0 +1,255 @@
+"""Offline PyPTO adapters: retain raw evidence, join by core/PC, never infer scores."""
+import collections
+import copy
+import csv
+import hashlib
+import html
+import json
+from pathlib import Path
+import struct
+
+VENDOR = Path(__file__).parent / 'vendor/pypto'
+
+
+def read(path):
+    return json.loads(Path(path).read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
+
+
+def save(path, value):
+    Path(path).write_text(json.dumps(value, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2) + '\n', encoding='utf-8')
+
+
+def fingerprint(path):
+    path = Path(path).resolve()
+    return dict(path=str(path), sha256=hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest())
+
+
+def verify_vendor():
+    manifest = read(VENDOR / 'provenance.json')
+    for item in manifest['files']:
+        if fingerprint(VENDOR / item['file'])['sha256'] != item['sha256']:
+            raise ValueError('vendored source changed: ' + item['file'])
+    return manifest['revision']
+
+
+def pc_key(value):
+    if value is None:
+        return None
+    return hex(int(value, 16) if isinstance(value, str) else int(value))
+
+
+def blocks(data):
+    """Validate complete framing before the upstream parser strips padding/path."""
+    from vendor.pypto import clean_sim_trace as upstream
+    offset = 0
+    while offset < len(data):
+        if len(data) - offset < 12:
+            raise ValueError('truncated block header')
+        size = struct.unpack_from('<Q', data, offset)[0]
+        if size > len(data) - offset - 12:
+            raise ValueError('truncated block payload')
+        offset += 12 + size
+    result = list(upstream.iter_blocks(data))
+    counts = collections.Counter(k for k, _ in result)
+    if counts[2] != 1 or counts[4] > 1:
+        raise ValueError('expected exactly one TRACE and at most one API_INSTR block')
+    return result
+
+
+def bind_identity(path, archive=None, binary=None, trace_hash=None):
+    identity = read(path) if path else {}
+    claimed = identity.get('trace_sha256')
+    if claimed and claimed != trace_hash:
+        raise ValueError('capture identity trace hash mismatch')
+    result = dict(record=fingerprint(path) if path else None, claims=identity,
+                  capture_link='recorded_by_collector' if path else 'unavailable', verified_files={})
+    for name, artifact, expected in [
+        ('source_archive', archive, identity.get('source_archive_sha256') or identity.get('source_sha256')),
+        ('device_binary', binary, identity.get('binary_sha256'))]:
+        if artifact:
+            actual = fingerprint(artifact)
+            if not expected or expected != actual['sha256']:
+                raise ValueError(name + ' hash missing or mismatched')
+            result['verified_files'][name] = actual
+    return result
+
+
+def signature(event):
+    return (event.get('pid'), event['name'], event['ts'], event.get('dur'),
+            pc_key(event.get('args', {}).get('pc_addr')))
+
+
+def audit_fidelity(raw, clean, keep_scalar):
+    from vendor.pypto import clean_sim_trace as upstream
+    expected = [e for e in raw['traceEvents'] if e.get('ph') == 'X'
+                and e.get('tid') not in upstream._DROP_LANES and e['name'] not in upstream._SYNC_NAMES
+                and (keep_scalar or e.get('tid') != 'SCALAR')]
+    actual = [e for e in clean['traceEvents'] if e.get('ph') == 'X']
+    if collections.Counter(map(signature, expected)) != collections.Counter(map(signature, actual)):
+        raise ValueError('cleaner altered retained instruction identity/timing')
+    lanes = collections.defaultdict(list)
+    for e in actual:
+        lanes[e['pid'], e['tid']].append(e)
+    for events in lanes.values():
+        events.sort(key=lambda e: e['ts'])
+        if any(a['ts'] + a.get('dur', 0) > b['ts'] + 1e-10 for a, b in zip(events, events[1:])):
+            raise ValueError('overlap remains inside a split display lane')
+    return dict(retained_events=len(actual), identities_and_times_unchanged=True, split_lanes_nonoverlapping=True)
+
+
+def join_metrics(clean, metrics):
+    events = collections.defaultdict(list)
+    for e in clean['traceEvents']:
+        if e.get('ph') == 'X':
+            events[e['pid'], pc_key(e.get('args', {}).get('pc_addr'))].append(e)
+    rows = []
+    for core, instructions in metrics.get('instructions', {}).items():
+        for r in instructions:
+            if r.get('instructions_executed', 0) <= 0:
+                continue
+            pc = pc_key(r.get('address'))
+            matched = events.get((core, pc), []) if pc is not None else []
+            mnemonic = str(r.get('source', '')).split(' ', 1)[0]
+            row = dict(core=core, pc=pc, instruction=mnemonic, pipe=r.get('pipe'),
+                executions=r['instructions_executed'], trace_events=len(matched), cycles=r.get('cycles'),
+                first_us=min((e['ts'] for e in matched), default=None),
+                last_us=max((e['ts'] + e.get('dur', 0) for e in matched), default=None),
+                first_operands=matched[0].get('args', {}).get('detail') if matched else None,
+                source_annotation=r.get('ascendc_inner_code') or None,
+                diagnostic='parser_semantics_suspect' if mnemonic == 'VAXPY' else 'model_not_hardware_pmu')
+            for key, target in [('ub_read_conflict', 'ub_read_conflict_model'),
+                                ('ub_write_conflict', 'ub_write_conflict_model'),
+                                ('vector_utilization_percentage', 'vector_payload_percentage')]:
+                value = r.get(key)
+                row[target] = value if isinstance(value, (int, float)) and value >= 0 else None
+            rows.append(row)
+    return rows
+
+
+CAVEATS = [
+    '模拟 cycle / 时间不是板上耗时或官方分数；指令区间可能包含排队，不能相加成关键路径。',
+    '清洗图隐藏 WAIT/SET/BAR，必须同时看 trace.raw.json；箭头仅重建已匹配的 flag，不是完整依赖图。',
+    '拆分泳道是显示层处理，不代表额外硬件 pipe；保留的指令时间、PC 和操作数不改变。',
+    'UB conflict 是解析器诊断模型；VAXPY 的 XM 操作数解释存在疑点，不能据此直接调整 padding。',
+    'vector_payload_percentage 是相对最大 repeat 载荷的比例，不是管道忙碌率；负值保留为不可用。',
+    'API_INSTR.Source 是指令文本；AscendC Inner Code 非空也需核对调试构建和源码身份。',
+    'SOURCE 块存在与否不等于 PC 映射成立；本工具不伪造 PC → C++ → IR/Pass 的关联。',
+]
+
+
+def coverage_from_hardware(path, identity, observed):
+    if not path:
+        return dict(observed_aiv=observed, expected_aiv=None, complete=None)
+    hardware = read(path)
+    if not identity.get('binary_sha256') or hardware.get('binary_sha256') != identity['binary_sha256']:
+        raise ValueError('coverage hardware report binary mismatch')
+    if identity.get('tokens_override'):
+        raise ValueError('prefix capture cannot use original hardware launch coverage')
+    launches = [s for s in hardware['samples'] if s['case'] == identity.get('case')]
+    counts = {int(s['stages'][0]['Mix Block Num']) for s in launches if len(s['stages']) == 1}
+    if len(counts) != 1 or any(len(s['stages']) != 1 for s in launches):
+        raise ValueError('coverage needs one consistent single-kernel launch')
+    expected = counts.pop()
+    return dict(observed_aiv=observed, expected_aiv=expected, complete=observed == expected,
+                reference=fingerprint(path), basis='matching binary and case in separate hardware capture')
+
+
+def clean_capture(path, output, identity=None, archive=None, binary=None, keep_scalar=True, hardware=None):
+    revision = verify_vendor()
+    from vendor.pypto import clean_sim_trace as upstream
+    source = upstream._resolve_input(Path(path)).resolve()
+    data = source.read_bytes()
+    capture = dict(path=str(source), sha256=hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest())
+    binding = bind_identity(identity, archive, binary, capture['sha256'])
+    parsed = blocks(data)
+    raw = json.loads(next(v for k, v in parsed if k == 2))
+    clean, skipped = upstream.rebuild_trace(copy.deepcopy(raw), keep_scalar=keep_scalar)
+    fidelity = audit_fidelity(raw, clean, keep_scalar)
+    api = next((json.loads(v) for k, v in parsed if k == 4), None)
+    metrics = upstream.reshape_metrics(api) if api is not None else {'instructions': {}, 'cores': []}
+    joined = join_metrics(clean, metrics)
+    per_core = {}
+    for core in sorted({e['pid'] for e in raw['traceEvents'] if e.get('ph') == 'X'}):
+        events = [e for e in raw['traceEvents'] if e.get('pid') == core and e.get('ph') == 'X'
+                  and e.get('tid') not in upstream._DROP_LANES and e['name'] not in upstream._SYNC_NAMES]
+        if not events:
+            continue
+        start = min(e['ts'] for e in events)
+        finish = max(e['ts'] + e.get('dur', 0) for e in events)
+        per_core[core] = dict(first_us=start, last_us=finish, instruction_envelope_us=finish-start,
+            instruction_events=len(events), pipe_counts=dict(collections.Counter(e['tid'] for e in events)),
+            opcode_counts=dict(collections.Counter(e['name'] for e in events)))
+    report = dict(schema_version=1, kind='simulator', capture=capture, identity=binding,
+        upstream_revision=revision, keep_scalar=keep_scalar, fidelity=fidelity,
+        blocks=dict(collections.Counter(k for k, _ in parsed)), skipped_sync_arrows=skipped,
+        matched_flows=sum(e.get('ph') == 's' for e in clean['traceEvents']),
+        active_core_pc_records=len(joined), joined_records=sum(r['trace_events'] > 0 for r in joined),
+        capabilities=dict(instruction_metrics=api is not None, source_blocks=any(k == 1 for k, _ in parsed),
+            source_annotations=sum(bool(r['source_annotation']) for r in joined),
+            pc_to_cpp='unavailable', pc_to_ir_pass='unavailable'),
+        cores=per_core, caveats=CAVEATS, performance_claim=None)
+    report['coverage'] = coverage_from_hardware(hardware, binding['claims'],
+                                               sum('veccore' in str(k) for k in per_core))
+    output = Path(output)
+    output.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=False)
+    save(output / 'trace.raw.json', raw)
+    save(output / 'trace.clean.json', clean)
+    save(output / 'instr_metrics.json', metrics)
+    save(output / 'pc_metrics.json', joined)
+    if joined:
+        with (output / 'pc_metrics.csv').open('w', newline='', encoding='utf-8-sig') as f:
+            writer = csv.DictWriter(f, fieldnames=list(joined[0]))
+            writer.writeheader(); writer.writerows(joined)
+    if identity:
+        (output / 'capture_identity.json').write_bytes(Path(identity).read_bytes())
+    report['outputs'] = {p.name: fingerprint(p)['sha256'] for p in output.iterdir() if p.is_file()}
+    save(output / 'evidence.json', report)
+    summary = ''.join(f'<li>{html.escape(c)}</li>' for c in CAVEATS)
+    links = ''.join(f'<li><a href="{n}">{n}</a></li>' for n in report['outputs'])
+    (output / 'index.html').write_text('<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Trace evidence</title>'
+        '<style>body{font:16px system-ui;max-width:1000px;margin:40px auto;line-height:1.7}</style>'
+        '<h1>Trace 证据包</h1><p>按同一 capture 的 core＋PC 关联；时间单位 µs。</p>'
+        f'<p>采集 SHA256：{capture["sha256"]}</p><ul>{links}</ul><ul>{summary}</ul>'
+        '<p>PC→C++→IR/Pass 尚无自动映射。evidence.json 记录实际能力和缺口。</p>', encoding='utf-8')
+    return dict(output=str(output.resolve()), capture_sha256=capture['sha256'], fidelity=fidelity,
+                active_core_pc_records=len(joined), capabilities=report['capabilities'], coverage=report['coverage'])
+
+
+def inspect_pc(directory, core, pc):
+    directory = Path(directory)
+    evidence = read(directory / 'evidence.json')
+    for name in ('pc_metrics.json', 'trace.raw.json'):
+        if fingerprint(directory / name)['sha256'] != evidence['outputs'][name]:
+            raise ValueError('evidence output changed: ' + name)
+    key = pc_key(pc)
+    return dict(capture=evidence['capture'], identity=evidence['identity'], core=core, pc=key,
+        metrics=[r for r in read(directory / 'pc_metrics.json') if r['core'] == core and r['pc'] == key],
+        raw_events=[e for e in read(directory / 'trace.raw.json')['traceEvents']
+                    if e.get('pid') == core and pc_key(e.get('args', {}).get('pc_addr')) == key],
+        capabilities=evidence['capabilities'])
+
+
+def add_cli(sub):
+    trace = sub.add_parser('trace', help='Offline PyPTO trace and IR evidence tools')
+    commands = trace.add_subparsers(dest='trace_command', required=True)
+    p = commands.add_parser('clean')
+    p.add_argument('input', type=Path); p.add_argument('-o', '--output', type=Path, required=True)
+    p.add_argument('--identity', type=Path); p.add_argument('--source-archive', type=Path)
+    p.add_argument('--device-binary', type=Path); p.add_argument('--drop-scalar', action='store_true')
+    p.add_argument('--hardware-summary', type=Path, help='Check observed AIV count against matching profile_selected summary')
+    p = commands.add_parser('pc')
+    p.add_argument('directory', type=Path); p.add_argument('--core', required=True); p.add_argument('--pc', required=True)
+    p = commands.add_parser('ir')
+    p.add_argument('inputs', type=Path, nargs='+'); p.add_argument('--format', choices=['llvm', 'pypto'], required=True)
+    p.add_argument('-o', '--output', type=Path, required=True)
+    p.add_argument('--function', help='LLVM definition-name regex; displayed line numbers are excerpt-relative')
+
+
+def run(args):
+    if args.trace_command == 'clean':
+        return clean_capture(args.input, args.output, args.identity, args.source_archive,
+                             args.device_binary, not args.drop_scalar, args.hardware_summary)
+    if args.trace_command == 'pc':
+        return inspect_pc(args.directory, args.core, args.pc)
+    from ir_bridge import render_ir
+    return render_ir(args.inputs, args.output, args.format, args.function)
